= Test set — Technical =

== Performance estimate ==
After a system h is frozen, test risk is estimated as:

<pre>
R_test(h) = (1/n_test) Σ_i ℓ(h(x_i), y_i)
</pre>

Its uncertainty depends on sample size, dependence structure, metric, and sampling process.

== Adaptive reuse ==
If h is repeatedly modified after observing R_test, the final h is dependent on S_test.

The nominal test estimate is then no longer a simple independent estimate for the selected system.

== Benchmark setting ==
Public leaderboards create an adaptive multi-team search process.

Hidden/private tests, rolling benchmarks, fresh test data, or strict evaluation protocols can reduce but not eliminate adaptive evaluation problems.

